<title>USA: Four bidders for U.S. stockpiled rubber.</title>
<headline>Four bidders for U.S. stockpiled rubber.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Four companies bid for U.S. Stockpile rubber in the solicitation opened May 15, Stockpile said.</p>
<p>Fenley Trading, Cargill, H Heller and Co, and Intertex World Resources presented bids for a total of 94.585 million lbs of technically specified hevea rubber for $30,536,039.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
